[[32,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Position the vehicle on the ramp.</p><p>Ensure that the ignition key is in the\nOFF position, then disconnect the negative battery terminal.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Battery</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3235044\">A1B</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>Proceed with removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a>\n                                           .</p><p>1. Disconnect the electrical connection from the engine oil temperature\nsender unit.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Engine oil temperature sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236488\">K29</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Undo and remove the engine oil temperature sender unit.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Recover the engine oil which comes\nout in a suitable container.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2013782.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Place the engine oil temperature sender\nunit in its seating and tighten it to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>-</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Connect the electrical connection to the\nengine oil temperature sender unit.</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Connect the negative (-) battery terminal.</p><p>Remove the car from the ramps.</p>"]]